415 | fields | McClean Field #9 in 1863 | - | 1863-07 | hedged | McClean Field #9 was most likely pasture, with a woodlot to the south (McClean Grove), a stone wall to the west, and wood fences along Mummasburg Road and a farm lane to the east | At the time of the battle, McClean Field #9 was most likely a pasture >>> a farm lane to the east.
